(2703988, 375673, 63267, '<td valign="top">Oh I remember those days of the basic rider course.  I did the ERC a couple months back and had to use my own bike to do it with.  Not the same as using the 250''s they usually provide in the basic course, but still fun.  Great capture here!</td>', 'Oh I remember those days of the basic rider course.  I did the ERC a couple months back and had to use my own bike to do it with.  Not the same as using the 250''s they usually provide in the basic course, but still fun.  Great capture here!', '2006-08-07 19:37:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2703992, 375545, 63267, '<td valign="top">Love the way the hair stands up in this shot.  You should trade the bertha in on a Kite tube though.  Lots of fun with insane air that will really make for some good action shots!  Great capture!</td>', 'Love the way the hair stands up in this shot.  You should trade the bertha in on a Kite tube though.  Lots of fun with insane air that will really make for some good action shots!  Great capture!', '2006-08-07 19:38:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2704014, 375809, 60799, '<td valign="top">I very much hope that this is a fake fish and if it''s not I sincerely hope that this fish wasn''t injured doing this.  Even if you did go through the trouble of making sure he was ok when shooting this take after take. I think it''s very irresponsible to post something like this here, because you know that the lack or originality and creativity of many of the members will lead them to do similar shots where the subject may not be as lucky.  Nice photo, but poor ethical decision.  I would like to see future challenge rules implemented where shots like this that involve the "torture" of living subjects be immedetly DQ''d</td>', 'I very much hope that this is a fake fish and if it''s not I sincerely hope that this fish wasn''t injured doing this.  Even if you did go through the trouble of making sure he was ok when shooting this take after take. I think it''s very irresponsible to post something like this here, because you know that the lack or originality and creativity of many of the members will lead them to do similar shots where the subject may not be as lucky.  Nice photo, but poor ethical decision.  I would like to see future challenge rules implemented where shots like this that involve the "torture" of living subjects be immedetly DQ''d', '2006-08-07 19:49:02.000000', NULL, 1),
