(2705454, 375531, 23394, '<td valign="top">one of the best!  too bad he didn''t have both arms up.  great perspective, colors.  good luck!</td>', 'one of the best!  too bad he didn''t have both arms up.  great perspective, colors.  good luck!', '2006-08-08 08:13:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2705458, 375322, 23394, '<td valign="top">great shot.  shame about the lighting, as it leaves the image a bit flat.  this might have been better with a bw conversion and some work with the levels and curves.  it''s a shame when you have something this good to start with, but you don''t take full advantage of the advanced editing rules...</td>', 'great shot.  shame about the lighting, as it leaves the image a bit flat.  this might have been better with a bw conversion and some work with the levels and curves.  it''s a shame when you have something this good to start with, but you don''t take full advantage of the advanced editing rules...', '2006-08-08 08:15:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2705460, 374742, 23394, '<td valign="top">excellent shot!  you might want to revisit this with some layered mask editing to bring out some of the shadow detail, though.  good luck!</td>', 'excellent shot!  you might want to revisit this with some layered mask editing to bring out some of the shadow detail, though.  good luck!', '2006-08-08 08:17:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2705461, 375787, 23394, '<td valign="top">great idea!  too bad you couldn''t shoot this on a sunny day, where the sun light would make the water sparkle 1000 times more than the flash.  another key to improving this type of shot is to get your subject to be throwing their arms in the air as they come out of the water, and to be slightly spinning.</td>', 'great idea!  too bad you couldn''t shoot this on a sunny day, where the sun light would make the water sparkle 1000 times more than the flash.  another key to improving this type of shot is to get your subject to be throwing their arms in the air as they come out of the water, and to be slightly spinning.', '2006-08-08 08:20:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(2705469, 374375, 23394, '<td valign="top">fantastic composition!  +fave</td>', 'fantastic composition!  +fave', '2006-08-08 08:21:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2705470, 375809, 23394, '<td valign="top">this is definitely an improvement over this ;-)<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=248997" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/395/thumb/248997.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/395/thumb/248997.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/395/thumb/248997.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>i guess practice makes perfect...</td>', 'this is definitely an improvement over this ;-)  i guess practice makes perfect...', '2006-08-08 08:22:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(2705474, 375773, 23394, '<td valign="top">as much as i can appreciate the effort required to produce this shot, it doesn''t do anything for me aesthetically.  i just reminds me too much of images from my high school physics textbooks.  i won''t hold that against you, though.  maybe if you had put food coloring in the water, it might be more interesting...</td>', 'as much as i can appreciate the effort required to produce this shot, it doesn''t do anything for me aesthetically.  i just reminds me too much of images from my high school physics textbooks.  i won''t hold that against you, though.  maybe if you had put food coloring in the water, it might be more interesting...', '2006-08-08 08:24:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2705478, 373870, 23394, '<td valign="top">nice shot, though it looks like it needs a slight rotation.  one part of me says, "oh, what a joyous moment."  the other part of me says, "ahhg, does he know how many ducks crap in that water?"  lovely colors, great idea, good luck!</td>', 'nice shot, though it looks like it needs a slight rotation.  one part of me says, "oh, what a joyous moment."  the other part of me says, "ahhg, does he know how many ducks crap in that water?"  lovely colors, great idea, good luck!', '2006-08-08 08:27:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2705486, 375755, 23394, '<td valign="top">nice idea, but needs some work.  first, your autofocus picked up on the water.  that''s fine, but your dof is too shallow.  also, your metering, by picking up on the brightness of the water, left too much shadow on your subjects face.  lastly, your hue/sat adjustment did some funny things to the coloring on the water.  how can it be fixed?  simple.  take some test shots, review your histogram, then switch to manual mode, and adjust your av/tv until you are getting a perfect exposure.  next, focus on your subject not moving, then switch to manual focus.  now, you''re ready for a killer shot!</td>', 'nice idea, but needs some work.  first, your autofocus picked up on the water.  that''s fine, but your dof is too shallow.  also, your metering, by picking up on the brightness of the water, left too much shadow on your subjects face.  lastly, your hue/sat adjustment did some funny things to the coloring on the water.  how can it be fixed?  simple.  take some test shots, review your histogram, then switch to manual mode, and adjust your av/tv until you are getting a perfect exposure.  next, focus on your subject not moving, then switch to manual focus.  now, you''re ready for a killer shot!', '2006-08-08 08:31:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2705493, 374122, 50255, '<td valign="top">great shot.</td>', 'great shot.', '2006-08-08 08:35:00.000000', NULL, 1),
