(2716741, 375827, 31307, '<td valign="top">"How shallow is it, Timmy?"<br/>*crunch!*<br/>"Okay, thanks!  We''ll go down a little further to try for a better place."<br/> <br/>Heh heh.<br/> <br/>Very interesting shot.  It has a sort of "cliff hanger ending" pun half intended.  I want resolution: a splash, but he never falls.  Very cool.</td>', '"How shallow is it, Timmy?"*crunch!*"Okay, thanks!  We''ll go down a little further to try for a better place." Heh heh. Very interesting shot.  It has a sort of "cliff hanger ending" pun half intended.  I want resolution: a splash, but he never falls.  Very cool.', '2006-08-11 04:51:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716742, 374344, 52549, '<td valign="top">Very cool. You probably ended up with a BIG omelette ;-)</td>', 'Very cool. You probably ended up with a BIG omelette ;-)', '2006-08-11 04:51:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716743, 375591, 31307, '<td valign="top">Sweet framing.  Interesting choice of B/W.  I like it.</td>', 'Sweet framing.  Interesting choice of B/W.  I like it.', '2006-08-11 04:51:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716744, 375746, 16004, '<td valign="top">cute moggy.  not sure that it''s really a great example of stopped motion though; cat yawns normally last so long it doesn''t really require any magnificent sense of timing...  the angle is a bit unusual, which due to his (lovely) black coat makes it tricky to define his shape.  and the eyes look positively insane!  the fore and background (well the brown fabric) does work very well, and the colours are very visually nice.  it''s a good cat shot - 7.</td>', 'cute moggy.  not sure that it''s really a great example of stopped motion though; cat yawns normally last so long it doesn''t really require any magnificent sense of timing...  the angle is a bit unusual, which due to his (lovely) black coat makes it tricky to define his shape.  and the eyes look positively insane!  the fore and background (well the brown fabric) does work very well, and the colours are very visually nice.  it''s a good cat shot - 7.', '2006-08-11 04:52:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716745, 374999, 31307, '<td valign="top">Nice panning.</td>', 'Nice panning.', '2006-08-11 04:52:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716746, 375620, 31307, '<td valign="top">You might have a future career (current career?) in skateboard photography.  Looks just like those posters you see plastered all over skateshops or a shot in a magazine.  Well done getting that look and feel.</td>', 'You might have a future career (current career?) in skateboard photography.  Looks just like those posters you see plastered all over skateshops or a shot in a magazine.  Well done getting that look and feel.', '2006-08-11 04:54:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716747, 375441, 31307, '<td valign="top">Very cool idea.</td>', 'Very cool idea.', '2006-08-11 04:54:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716752, 375874, 16004, '<td valign="top">i think this is a pretty fancy shot.  the horse himself is brilliantly sharp and fantastically lit - his muscles are really enhanced by the natural light.  it''s a slight pity you didn''t get it JUST the moment all four hooves are in the air (just like that famous 100+ year old photo), and i might be tempted to make this black and white or sepia as a nod to that historic picture (you know the one; two guys bet about the horse ever leaving the ground, so set a long row of cameras taking shots as the horse passes and basically creates the first motion picture).  but i digress. this is a very nice.  7.</td>', 'i think this is a pretty fancy shot.  the horse himself is brilliantly sharp and fantastically lit - his muscles are really enhanced by the natural light.  it''s a slight pity you didn''t get it JUST the moment all four hooves are in the air (just like that famous 100+ year old photo), and i might be tempted to make this black and white or sepia as a nod to that historic picture (you know the one; two guys bet about the horse ever leaving the ground, so set a long row of cameras taking shots as the horse passes and basically creates the first motion picture).  but i digress. this is a very nice.  7.', '2006-08-11 05:08:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716753, 375771, 16004, '<td valign="top">taking a picture of something not moving isn''t really stopped motion; it''s just stopped.  it''s a nice (semi-classic) view of GCS, though it feels that to me the building is taking centre stage, rather than the non-desatted people. i do like that the people are almost dead centre (nice composition), but i think the selected desat doesn''t quite work here; maybe the greyscales aren''t dark or contrasty enough for max impact, or perhaps the people are just too small?  5.</td>', 'taking a picture of something not moving isn''t really stopped motion; it''s just stopped.  it''s a nice (semi-classic) view of GCS, though it feels that to me the building is taking centre stage, rather than the non-desatted people. i do like that the people are almost dead centre (nice composition), but i think the selected desat doesn''t quite work here; maybe the greyscales aren''t dark or contrasty enough for max impact, or perhaps the people are just too small?  5.', '2006-08-11 05:16:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716803, 375514, 4517, '<td valign="top">great picture love the way all the bulb bits are going in different directions it looks very good 9</td>', 'great picture love the way all the bulb bits are going in different directions it looks very good 9', '2006-08-11 05:56:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716825, 375881, 16004, '<td valign="top">my big wish for this picture is that the wonderful bokeh type background filled the whole image.  the white sky is so overpowering, that it just makes me feel mildly disappointed.  which isn''t to say you HAVEN''T done a great job here; the detail and capture of the bird is really super.  i think the bird could do with he white bits being made whiter (curves or dodge) but that aside, it''s lovely.  7.<br/> <br/>(editted to correct grammer from you''ve to haven''t!  sorry!)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-08-14 03:22:05.</i></td>', 'my big wish for this picture is that the wonderful bokeh type background filled the whole image.  the white sky is so overpowering, that it just makes me feel mildly disappointed.  which isn''t to say you HAVEN''T done a great job here; the detail and capture of the bird is really super.  i think the bird could do with he white bits being made whiter (curves or dodge) but that aside, it''s lovely.  7. (editted to correct grammer from you''ve to haven''t!  sorry!)', '2006-08-11 06:10:58.000000', '2006-08-14 04:22:05.000000', 1),
(2716885, 375688, 16004, '<td valign="top">the fact that the strawberry is covered in milk already kind of suggests that this is following a number of attempts to get it right, which kind of lessens the wow! impressed! factor.  if it was a clean virgin strawberry, then i think it would be more striking.  the other thing i would add is that the lighting seems to strong, pretty much wiping out the crown you get from the splosh.  it''s still a decent capture, nice and sharp, and certainly fits the challenge. 5.</td>', 'the fact that the strawberry is covered in milk already kind of suggests that this is following a number of attempts to get it right, which kind of lessens the wow! impressed! factor.  if it was a clean virgin strawberry, then i think it would be more striking.  the other thing i would add is that the lighting seems to strong, pretty much wiping out the crown you get from the splosh.  it''s still a decent capture, nice and sharp, and certainly fits the challenge. 5.', '2006-08-11 07:18:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716930, 374959, 23394, '<td valign="top">a nice enough capture, but compositionally, it doesn''t really blow me away.  these shots are tough, and i appreciate your effort.  i guess the thing that''s sticking me is that it''s not quite sharp enough for me to go "wow! you nailed it" or not quite blurry enough to consider it art (which, even though it would defeat the purpose of the challenge, would make for a cool shot).  maybe a square crop would strengthen the image, so as to keep it from feeling like the subject is on the cusp of flying out of the frame.</td>', 'a nice enough capture, but compositionally, it doesn''t really blow me away.  these shots are tough, and i appreciate your effort.  i guess the thing that''s sticking me is that it''s not quite sharp enough for me to go "wow! you nailed it" or not quite blurry enough to consider it art (which, even though it would defeat the purpose of the challenge, would make for a cool shot).  maybe a square crop would strengthen the image, so as to keep it from feeling like the subject is on the cusp of flying out of the frame.', '2006-08-11 07:47:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716931, 375351, 23394, '<td valign="top">beautiful colors, incredible clarity.</td>', 'beautiful colors, incredible clarity.', '2006-08-11 07:47:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716933, 375566, 23394, '<td valign="top">it''s highly unfortunate, but the muted background robs this image of life, for me, anyway.  technically, it''s an excellent shot, spot on for the challenge, but compositionally, it just doesn''t grab me.  maybe a tighter crop and a brighter, more contrasty background would have made it pop.</td>', 'it''s highly unfortunate, but the muted background robs this image of life, for me, anyway.  technically, it''s an excellent shot, spot on for the challenge, but compositionally, it just doesn''t grab me.  maybe a tighter crop and a brighter, more contrasty background would have made it pop.', '2006-08-11 07:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716934, 374973, 23394, '<td valign="top">nice idea, but a bit too soft.</td>', 'nice idea, but a bit too soft.', '2006-08-11 07:50:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716938, 375422, 23394, '<td valign="top">great subject, great idea.  too bad you didn''t enter one of him in air, above the can.  also, a vertical crop would have taken out the unnecessary background at the right of the frame.</td>', 'great subject, great idea.  too bad you didn''t enter one of him in air, above the can.  also, a vertical crop would have taken out the unnecessary background at the right of the frame.', '2006-08-11 07:51:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716941, 375917, 23394, '<td valign="top">nice idea, but a bit soft.  tough lighting situation as well.  this image definitely has its place, even though it''s probably sitting mid-range for the challenge.</td>', 'nice idea, but a bit soft.  tough lighting situation as well.  this image definitely has its place, even though it''s probably sitting mid-range for the challenge.', '2006-08-11 07:52:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716943, 374036, 23394, '<td valign="top">nice idea, but something about it just doesn''t grab me.  maybe it just needs a bit more water.<br/> <br/>[also, it looks like you have a smudge at the top left of your lens]</td>', 'nice idea, but something about it just doesn''t grab me.  maybe it just needs a bit more water. [also, it looks like you have a smudge at the top left of your lens]', '2006-08-11 07:53:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716944, 375623, 23394, '<td valign="top">nice idea, but a bit too soft.  also, compositionally, it would have been stronger had you positioned yourself to shoot without the pole being so prominent.</td>', 'nice idea, but a bit too soft.  also, compositionally, it would have been stronger had you positioned yourself to shoot without the pole being so prominent.', '2006-08-11 07:54:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716947, 375803, 23394, '<td valign="top">nice idea, but a bit soft.  also, this really should have been cropped vertically so that the ball wouldn''t be so hard to find.  this is a nice perspective to shoot from; be wary, though, of your backgrounds.  even though they are largely out of your control, do what you can to mitigate their impact.  here, moving to the right of the ump and shooting from a higher perspective (maybe holding camera over your head and shooting down) would have removed most of the cars from the frame.</td>', 'nice idea, but a bit soft.  also, this really should have been cropped vertically so that the ball wouldn''t be so hard to find.  this is a nice perspective to shoot from; be wary, though, of your backgrounds.  even though they are largely out of your control, do what you can to mitigate their impact.  here, moving to the right of the ump and shooting from a higher perspective (maybe holding camera over your head and shooting down) would have removed most of the cars from the frame.', '2006-08-11 07:57:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716948, 375840, 23394, '<td valign="top">nice idea.  love the background sky.  just wish you had composed it so that the man''s arm didn''t get lost in the boy.  also, it could have been a wee bit sharper.</td>', 'nice idea.  love the background sky.  just wish you had composed it so that the man''s arm didn''t get lost in the boy.  also, it could have been a wee bit sharper.', '2006-08-11 07:57:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716951, 375898, 23394, '<td valign="top">like the colors, appreciate the effort.  this is one of the better of its ilk.  if you had been able to throw a little light from the bottom, it would even be better.</td>', 'like the colors, appreciate the effort.  this is one of the better of its ilk.  if you had been able to throw a little light from the bottom, it would even be better.', '2006-08-11 07:59:22.000000', NULL, 1),
