(2718307, 375358, 30049, '<td valign="top">This youngster looks happy!  ;^)  Fun image you''ve captured here.  Couple of minor things to throw at you; 1) seems to be a blueish cast to the image - may want to check the color temp or your white balance 2) shutter speed wasn''t quite quick enough to stop all motion as the feet are blurry.  Other than that - nice capture.  All of the above is obviously JMO of course.  ;^)  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'This youngster looks happy!  ;^)  Fun image you''ve captured here.  Couple of minor things to throw at you; 1) seems to be a blueish cast to the image - may want to check the color temp or your white balance 2) shutter speed wasn''t quite quick enough to stop all motion as the feet are blurry.  Other than that - nice capture.  All of the above is obviously JMO of course.  ;^)  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-08-11 16:20:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718315, 374302, 30049, '<td valign="top">You''re funny!  ;^)  Should have had some rotten tomatoes already on his shirt.  You''ve done a nice job of capturing the water and stopping the motion with the correct shutter speed.  Lighting is good and the focus is right on the mark.  Overall, well done!  Humor should buy you a point or two...he-he.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'You''re funny!  ;^)  Should have had some rotten tomatoes already on his shirt.  You''ve done a nice job of capturing the water and stopping the motion with the correct shutter speed.  Lighting is good and the focus is right on the mark.  Overall, well done!  Humor should buy you a point or two...he-he.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-08-11 16:23:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718321, 375809, 42495, '<td valign="top">Real clever shot and I have no idea how you did it, other than making the poor fishy jump!  Good stopped motion and composition.  White background is effective.</td>', 'Real clever shot and I have no idea how you did it, other than making the poor fishy jump!  Good stopped motion and composition.  White background is effective.', '2006-08-11 16:25:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718323, 375205, 30049, '<td valign="top">Pretty bird...nice panning shot.  Only bummer is that the bird isn''t really in focus as you have some blur on the bird.  So close!  Panning shots are difficult to achieve without blurring the subject.  I do like the rich color in the background.  It really helps make the white bird stand out.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'Pretty bird...nice panning shot.  Only bummer is that the bird isn''t really in focus as you have some blur on the bird.  So close!  Panning shots are difficult to achieve without blurring the subject.  I do like the rich color in the background.  It really helps make the white bird stand out.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2006-08-11 16:25:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718328, 375847, 30049, '<td valign="top">Well composed with the bird flying into the frame.  Good detail on the bird as it''s well focused and not blurred at all.  I think the only thing that''s going to hurt you is the chosen subject...there are a lot of seagull shots.  Not saying that''s right or wrong...just making an observation.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'Well composed with the bird flying into the frame.  Good detail on the bird as it''s well focused and not blurred at all.  I think the only thing that''s going to hurt you is the chosen subject...there are a lot of seagull shots.  Not saying that''s right or wrong...just making an observation.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2006-08-11 16:27:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718332, 375853, 30049, '<td valign="top">Oh yeah...here we go.  Well done!  Great composition.  Good focus.  Lighting is on the money.  Cool background with the cloudy sky, and hey, get this...no motion blur!  Hooray!  ;^)  Should see this one on the front page come rollover on Monday.  Congrats in advance!</td>', 'Oh yeah...here we go.  Well done!  Great composition.  Good focus.  Lighting is on the money.  Cool background with the cloudy sky, and hey, get this...no motion blur!  Hooray!  ;^)  Should see this one on the front page come rollover on Monday.  Congrats in advance!', '2006-08-11 16:29:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718341, 375577, 30049, '<td valign="top">Clever title to a well shot image.  Several duck/water shots in here.  You''ve captured this one with some nice lighting, no motion blur, and the image is well focused.  Job well done.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Clever title to a well shot image.  Several duck/water shots in here.  You''ve captured this one with some nice lighting, no motion blur, and the image is well focused.  Job well done.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-08-11 16:30:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718345, 374934, 30049, '<td valign="top">Wow!  That''s sharp!  Great detail in the face, eyes, and beak.  Would like to see it a bit brighter...feels a tad underexposed.  But that''s my only real complaint.   Nice job and good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Wow!  That''s sharp!  Great detail in the face, eyes, and beak.  Would like to see it a bit brighter...feels a tad underexposed.  But that''s my only real complaint.   Nice job and good luck in the challenge.', '2006-08-11 16:31:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718354, 375820, 30049, '<td valign="top">It''s ok.  My first impression.  Sorry.  The image is technically fine overall, but nothing giving that ''wow'' impression.  Know what I mean?  Not that you have much control over the background in this scenario, but I think for this image to really work the player should be a little more isolate.  JMO of course.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'It''s ok.  My first impression.  Sorry.  The image is technically fine overall, but nothing giving that ''wow'' impression.  Know what I mean?  Not that you have much control over the background in this scenario, but I think for this image to really work the player should be a little more isolate.  JMO of course.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2006-08-11 16:34:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718359, 375882, 30049, '<td valign="top">Wonderful bird.  You''ve stopped the motion just fine.  The image overall feels quite flat like you need some additional contrast.  The subject is also on the soft side, a little sharpening would probably really make this eagle stand out.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Wonderful bird.  You''ve stopped the motion just fine.  The image overall feels quite flat like you need some additional contrast.  The subject is also on the soft side, a little sharpening would probably really make this eagle stand out.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-08-11 16:35:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718364, 375417, 30049, '<td valign="top">Smooth.  That''s the first impression I get.  You''ve stopped the motion just fine.  This image feels kind of documentary.  Like it belongs in a book or website with a description of the plane underneath.  Not a bad thing overall, just not a ''wow - this is exciting'' reaction to this image.  Sorry.  JMO of course.  ;^)  Best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'Smooth.  That''s the first impression I get.  You''ve stopped the motion just fine.  This image feels kind of documentary.  Like it belongs in a book or website with a description of the plane underneath.  Not a bad thing overall, just not a ''wow - this is exciting'' reaction to this image.  Sorry.  JMO of course.  ;^)  Best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2006-08-11 16:37:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718373, 375637, 59215, '<td valign="top">Nice image, but I''m not sure I like the effects... has a paste/plastic feel to it.</td>', 'Nice image, but I''m not sure I like the effects... has a paste/plastic feel to it.', '2006-08-11 16:43:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718476, 375901, 57745, '<td valign="top">wow! great shot... i like the composition of this photo. i like the way how the principles of line applied to create a dynamic picture. only if you show another blind to hold on, this would be perfect... goodluck!</td>', 'wow! great shot... i like the composition of this photo. i like the way how the principles of line applied to create a dynamic picture. only if you show another blind to hold on, this would be perfect... goodluck!', '2006-08-11 17:08:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718486, 374999, 41337, '<td valign="top">The composition/angle you used really adds something extra to this photo. I love how the lines slice through the image diagonally and even frames it sorta like a scrapbook would. The color is also very good but not over the top. If I were to find any faults with this, which I don''t it would be the dark line above the car. I''d probably have cloned that out to make it cleaner looking for finicky voter.</td>', 'The composition/angle you used really adds something extra to this photo. I love how the lines slice through the image diagonally and even frames it sorta like a scrapbook would. The color is also very good but not over the top. If I were to find any faults with this, which I don''t it would be the dark line above the car. I''d probably have cloned that out to make it cleaner looking for finicky voter.', '2006-08-11 17:10:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718488, 375614, 41337, '<td valign="top">Love the square crop. That''s got to be one of the thickest cat tongues I''ve every seen although I''m sure it''s just the angle of it.</td>', 'Love the square crop. That''s got to be one of the thickest cat tongues I''ve every seen although I''m sure it''s just the angle of it.', '2006-08-11 17:12:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718492, 375827, 33552, '<td valign="top">Great colors and timing, but it seems like you''re trying to get alot in here. If the cliff is the subject, the vertical composition makes sense, but I would like to see the rock face properly exposed. If the diver is the subject (as I believe he is here) perhaps a horizontal (or square) composition would work better to emphasize the movement and position of the diver. Still, a very nice shot.</td>', 'Great colors and timing, but it seems like you''re trying to get alot in here. If the cliff is the subject, the vertical composition makes sense, but I would like to see the rock face properly exposed. If the diver is the subject (as I believe he is here) perhaps a horizontal (or square) composition would work better to emphasize the movement and position of the diver. Still, a very nice shot.', '2006-08-11 17:14:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718499, 374700, 41337, '<td valign="top">Very unusual image. I like the idea and the execution is good but the image suffers a bit from quality. The detail is there but so is some funky stuff. Judging by the file size (only 25k) it''s probably jpg compression which is a shame since you could have probably saved this at a 100% without reaching the 150k limit. Other than that it''s excellent. The composition the background and the stop motion.</td>', 'Very unusual image. I like the idea and the execution is good but the image suffers a bit from quality. The detail is there but so is some funky stuff. Judging by the file size (only 25k) it''s probably jpg compression which is a shame since you could have probably saved this at a 100% without reaching the 150k limit. Other than that it''s excellent. The composition the background and the stop motion.', '2006-08-11 17:17:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718541, 375911, 41337, '<td valign="top">Returning for comments.<br/> <br/>There appears to be a bit of a color cast going on (red). Assuming you have photoshop, a simple curves adjustment using just the options: Find Dark &amp; Light Colors would have corrected it. Also, adding a bit more contrast using the unsharp mask technique would have helped give this image more oomph, IMO. In other words, apply unsharp mask with settings along these lines: Amount = 18, Radius = 40, Threshold = 1 and experiment from there. <br/> <br/>In terms of improvements in camera, I think an angle that got more of her face in the shot rather than this side view would have given this more impact as well as shooting even lower to the ground. You would get more of the crashing waves in the shot which add/heighten the drama in the scene. <br/> <br/>Anyway, just some thoughts. Good luck!</td>', 'Returning for comments. There appears to be a bit of a color cast going on (red). Assuming you have photoshop, a simple curves adjustment using just the options: Find Dark & Light Colors would have corrected it. Also, adding a bit more contrast using the unsharp mask technique would have helped give this image more oomph, IMO. In other words, apply unsharp mask with settings along these lines: Amount = 18, Radius = 40, Threshold = 1 and experiment from there.  In terms of improvements in camera, I think an angle that got more of her face in the shot rather than this side view would have given this more impact as well as shooting even lower to the ground. You would get more of the crashing waves in the shot which add/heighten the drama in the scene.  Anyway, just some thoughts. Good luck!', '2006-08-11 17:28:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718550, 375426, 25742, '<td valign="top">love the expression on the guy in yellow</td>', 'love the expression on the guy in yellow', '2006-08-11 17:30:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718556, 375637, 25742, '<td valign="top">stopped motion?</td>', 'stopped motion?', '2006-08-11 17:31:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718558, 375875, 25742, '<td valign="top">refreshing :)</td>', 'refreshing :)', '2006-08-11 17:33:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718563, 375678, 41337, '<td valign="top">Returning for comments.<br/> <br/>You shoot this right before the Fire challenge? That sucks. :P Well, if you decide to shoot something similar for the fire challenge I would suggest trying to improve the way you are lighting this. The harsh light on the right needs to be diffused so it doesn''t create that hot spot. Maybe use some white sheets double folded if you are using a a make shift setup. Also, add some diffused fill light to the front of that cigarette or whatever that is. If you''ve seen others shoot matches like this they always light the tip so you can see the texture detail which has a very appealing quality. If you are going for something different then try just lighting the smoke and flame only and avoid any hot spots on the cigarette. That''s the main issue here with this photo. That and also the noise. It doesn''t bother me but I wouldn''t expect others to like it so much.</td>', 'Returning for comments. You shoot this right before the Fire challenge? That sucks. :P Well, if you decide to shoot something similar for the fire challenge I would suggest trying to improve the way you are lighting this. The harsh light on the right needs to be diffused so it doesn''t create that hot spot. Maybe use some white sheets double folded if you are using a a make shift setup. Also, add some diffused fill light to the front of that cigarette or whatever that is. If you''ve seen others shoot matches like this they always light the tip so you can see the texture detail which has a very appealing quality. If you are going for something different then try just lighting the smoke and flame only and avoid any hot spots on the cigarette. That''s the main issue here with this photo. That and also the noise. It doesn''t bother me but I wouldn''t expect others to like it so much.', '2006-08-11 17:34:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2718586, 374999, 25742, '<td valign="top">superb pan. the tilt fits, somehow. best of luck</td>', 'superb pan. the tilt fits, somehow. best of luck', '2006-08-11 17:41:09.000000', NULL, 1),
