(2744729, 375441, 9906, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club:<br/> <br/>This is a different take on the challenge.  I''m not sure I really like it, but it is what it is.<br/> <br/>The flames ''coming out of'' the barrel of the gun don''t look right.  Too much color.  Too many different colors.  You have a bullet that isn''t a bullet, it''s a shell with the bullet still inside.  The color of lighting on the face and hand don''t match the color of lighting of the bullet and flames.  The facial expressions of the model on the left look forced.  The hand holding the gun is at an odd angle to the wrist.  Put all these together and I think it explains the score that you recieved.<br/> <br/>My personal oppinion:  This looks too much like digital art and not enough like photography for me.  Nothing personal, just MHO.<br/> <br/>Yours<br/>TC</td>', 'From the Critique Club: This is a different take on the challenge.  I''m not sure I really like it, but it is what it is. The flames ''coming out of'' the barrel of the gun don''t look right.  Too much color.  Too many different colors.  You have a bullet that isn''t a bullet, it''s a shell with the bullet still inside.  The color of lighting on the face and hand don''t match the color of lighting of the bullet and flames.  The facial expressions of the model on the left look forced.  The hand holding the gun is at an odd angle to the wrist.  Put all these together and I think it explains the score that you recieved. My personal oppinion:  This looks too much like digital art and not enough like photography for me.  Nothing personal, just MHO. YoursTC', '2006-08-21 00:46:47.000000', NULL, 0),
